---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  role="visitor"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: "Home", href: "/" },
    { label: "Methods & quality" },
    { label: "Data collection" },
  ]}
  backHref="/methods/evaluation-framework"
>
  <div class="mx-auto px-4 py-8 max-w-4xl prose prose-gray">
    <h1>How the Data is Collected</h1>

    <section>
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        Data collection in the SUM platform follows a structured process designed to ensure
        consistency across all participating cities. Each city (Living Lab or Contributing city)
        follows the same collection methodology, enabling meaningful comparison and aggregation
        of results at the European level.
      </p>
      <p>
        For full details on the collection process and available tools, visit the
        <a href="/data/collection-plan" class="text-primary hover:underline">Data collection process page</a> or
        the <a href="/methods/evaluation-framework" class="text-primary hover:underline">Evaluation framework</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The 4-step collection process</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Baseline measurement</strong> — Cities collect KPI values before implementing
          any mobility measures. This establishes the reference point for impact assessment.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Measure implementation</strong> — Cities implement one or more mobility measures
          (push or pull) and document them in the platform.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Post-implementation measurement</strong> — After a defined observation period,
          cities collect KPI values again using the same methodology as baseline.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Validation and submission</strong> — Collected data is reviewed by the consortium
          data team before being accepted into the platform and made available for analysis.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Available resources for data collectors</h2>
      <p>
        The platform provides several tools to support cities during data collection:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>KPI calculation spreadsheet templates</li>
        <li>Survey instruments for qualitative KPI measurement</li>
        <li>Guidance documentation for each KPI</li>
        <li>A dedicated data collection process guide</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        All resources are available in the
        <a href="/tools/resources" class="text-primary hover:underline">Resource library</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Why your data matters</h2>
      <p>
        Each city's data contribution strengthens the platform's ability to identify patterns
        across European contexts. The more cities contribute data, the more robust the impact
        analysis and MCDA recommendations become. Data is anonymised where appropriate and
        governed by the consortium's data sharing agreement.
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="not-prose mt-8 flex gap-4 text-sm">
      <a href="/methods/data-quality" class="text-primary hover:underline">Next: Data quality →</a>
      <a href="/data/collection-plan" class="text-primary hover:underline">Collection plan details →</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</Layout>
